## What Cascade Must Do (Per Protocol)

### STEP 1: INITIALIZATION

- Read `.agent/MANDATORY_SESSION_PROTOCOL.md` **INCLUDING Protocol Violations Log section**
- Read `.agent/active-context.md` and `.agent/progress.md` (current phase)
- Read `docs/13-Project-Plan.md` and `docs/12-Backlog.md`
- Create `.agent/task/current-session-[YYYYMMDD-HHMM].md`
- **Confirm:** `✅ STEP 1 COMPLETE: Session initialized at [timestamp]`

**Reading Path After Step 1**

- **Implementation phases:** `docs/03-Architecture.md` → `docs/04-Data-and-Model-Spec.md` → `docs/06-API/openapi.yaml`
- **Planning phases:** `docs/01-PRD.md` → `docs/02-SRS.md` → `docs/12-Backlog.md`

(See `docs/README.md` for full reading paths.)

### STEP 2: PLAN CREATION

- Create an implementation plan (use ExitPlanMode if helpful).
- Obtain user approval.
- **Immediately save** plan to `.agent/task/current-plan.md`.
- Create `.agent/task/current-todos.md`.
- **Confirm:** `✅ STEP 2 COMPLETE: Plan saved to current-plan.md, todos saved to current-todos.md`.

### STEP 3: EXPERT CONSULTATION

- Invoke `react-expert` for component architecture.
- Invoke `next-js-expert` for Server/Client and data fetching decisions.
- Invoke `prisma-expert` for database schema and query optimization.
- **Confirm:** `✅ STEP 3 COMPLETE: Consulted [expert-name] for [decision-topic]`.

**When experts are required**

- New component architectures or complex UI flows.
- Complex backend features or performance-sensitive areas.
- Any database schema changes or non-trivial Prisma queries.

**When experts are optional**

- Routine CRUD following established patterns.
- Minor UI updates that match existing conventions.
- Small refactors within an established module.

### STEP 4: PROGRESS CHECKPOINTS

- At 15K, 30K, 45K, 60K, 75K, 90K tokens:
  - Update `.agent/task/current-session.md`.
  - Update `.agent/task/current-todos.md`.
- **Confirm:** `✅ CHECKPOINT at [X]K tokens: Progress saved`.

### STEP 4.5: VERIFICATION GATE (EVIDENCE-BASED)

**CRITICAL**: This step was violated on 2025-11-10. See Protocol Violations Log.

**Before marking ANY work complete:**

- Re-read `.agent/task/current-plan.md` success criteria
- Verify EACH requirement with concrete evidence:
  - **Files**: Run `ls` commands, show output
  - **TypeScript**: Run `npx tsc --noEmit`, show clean output
  - **HTTP Endpoints**: Run `curl` commands, show 200 OK status
  - **Database**: Run queries, show counts
  - **Tests**: Run tests, show passing results
- **Document ALL verification evidence in session file**
- Create verification summary table with Expected/Actual/Status columns
- **Fail-fast rule**: If ANY requirement fails → mark incomplete, continue work
- Only proceed to Step 5 when ALL verified WITH EVIDENCE

**Required Confirmation:**
```
✅ STEP 4.5 COMPLETE: All verification criteria passed with documented evidence

Verification Results:
| Criterion | Expected | Actual | Status |
|-----------|----------|--------|--------|
| [item 1]  | [expect] | [actual] | ✅ PASS |
| [item 2]  | [expect] | [actual] | ✅ PASS |

Evidence documented in: .agent/task/current-session-[timestamp].md
```

See `.agent/MANDATORY_SESSION_PROTOCOL.md` Step 4.5 for detailed examples and Protocol Violations Log.

### STEP 5: POST-COMPLETION WORKFLOW

**CRITICAL**: This step was violated on 2025-11-10. See Protocol Violations Log.

**After feature implementation complete, BEFORE committing code:**

#### 5.1: Update Project Documentation (REQUIRED)

- [ ] Update `docs/13-Project-Plan.md`:
  - Mark completed user stories (e.g., US-016, US-017 complete)
  - Add status tracking section with progress percentage
  - Document quality metrics (TypeScript errors, HTTP status, tests)
- [ ] Update `docs/12-Backlog.md` (ONLY if scope changed)

#### 5.2: Update Memory Banks (REQUIRED)

- [ ] Update `.agent/active-context.md` (current focus for next session)
- [ ] Update `.agent/progress.md` (milestone completion, lessons learned)
- [ ] Update `.agent/system-patterns.md` (if new patterns)
- [ ] Update `.agent/tech-context.md` (if stack changed)

#### 5.3: Invoke Sub-Agents (REQUIRED if applicable)

- [ ] **If new patterns created**: Invoke `synthesize-docs` sub-agent
  - Generates SOPs from implemented patterns
  - Saves to `.agent/sops/[pattern-name].md`
  - Updates `.agent/README.md` index
- [ ] **If architecture changed**: Invoke `map-system` sub-agent
  - Updates `.agent/system/api-catalog.md` (if new endpoints)
  - Updates `.agent/system/database-schema.md` (if schema changed)
  - Updates `.agent/system/component-patterns.md` (if new components)

#### 5.4: Commit Documentation (REQUIRED)

- [ ] **Documentation commit FIRST**: `git add .agent/ docs/ && git commit -m "docs: ..."`
- [ ] **Code commit SECOND**: `git add [code files] && git commit -m "feat: ..."`
- [ ] **Push**: `git push origin [branch]`

**Required Confirmation:**
```
✅ STEP 5 COMPLETE: All post-completion workflow tasks executed

Project docs updated:
- docs/13-Project-Plan.md (US-XXX marked complete, status tracking added)
- docs/12-Backlog.md (no changes - scope unchanged)

Memory banks updated:
- .agent/active-context.md (next session focus)
- .agent/progress.md (milestone complete, metrics updated)

Sub-agents invoked:
- synthesize-docs: Created [N] SOPs ([X] lines total)
- map-system: Updated component-patterns.md ([N] new patterns)

Git commits:
- Documentation: [commit hash] "docs: ..."
- Code (if applicable): [commit hash] "feat: ..."
- Pushed to origin/[branch]
```

**If you cannot provide ALL these updates, Step 5 is NOT complete.**

